# debug.keystore is intentionally NOT ignored - see below.
# This is the DEBUG signing key only (never the release key), and it must be
# committed and stay identical across every CI build. If this file is missing,
# CI generates a brand new random keystore on every run, which re-signs the APK
# with a different key each time - Android then refuses to install the update
# over the previous one ("package conflicts with an existing package") and
# forces the user to uninstall first. Debug keystores use a universally known,
# non-secret password ("android"/"android"), so committing this file is safe
# and standard practice - it is NOT the same as committing a release keystore.
